# Line endings.
#
# Git normalises text files to LF in the repository; these rules decide what a checkout gets back.
# The files a Linux shell, nginx or Docker reads have to be LF even in a Windows working copy: a CRLF
# in a Dockerfile turns a "\" line continuation into a literal character and breaks the build, and a
# CRLF in an .envsh leaves a carriage return on the end of every value the entrypoint sets.
#
# Anything not listed is normalised by `* text=auto`, which leaves binaries such as the photographs
# alone.

* text=auto

*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.envsh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.template text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
